+# V17 bounded startup stage result export
+
+This version adds preparationStages once to the existing startup raw, alongside preparationSummary, using the same original prepareLighting Promise fulfilment side reaction. There is still one native.then call per original operation. No new wrapper, timer, polling, renderer/readiness/GPU call or product change. Original Promise/value/receiver/arguments/falsy errors are unchanged. The owner restores on terminal/abort/rejoin and retains only the closed scalar evidence after disposal.
+
+The closed projection exports original stage names, passQuality, elapsed/active/paused times, tick/check/render/restart counts, original CPU apply/checkBatch/render aggregates, rafGap aggregates and the14 known Game revision reasons plus revision-length. It never exports arbitrary strings, shaders, resources, user data or invented per-stage compiler counters. Limits are16quality passes,304rows and256KiB. Cumulative qualities.stageCount plus each stage.passQuality determines passIndex, including repeated Medium. Missing/invalid/partial/truncated layouts have explicit flags and null indices. Own data descriptors only; getters are not invoked. preparationStages is optional in legacy envelopes, accepted only on startup under the unchanged2MiB receipt cap.
+
+The two source14 recordings lost their original stage records to the existing recorder cap. This version cannot recover those missing values. A new immutable build and actual startup must supply future evidence; CPU tests are not GPU or performance acceptance.
+
+All36 original V16 files remain immutable. This new36file pack updates only observer/overlay/receipt, this README and copied tests. Copies retain behavioral/pin/order assertions, with explicit version-count/path corrections and exact normalization in historical test-byte guards. Old DOM bindings resolve today's imports; the buffer fixture supplies its missing query-error Observable; explicit post-ready shader-window behavior replaces an obsolete startup-window expectation while preserving original failure/inventory/restoration checks. Temp output is confined to this task. Public startup-stage-export evidence records the exact metadata changes, failures, guards and verification. The sections below document inherited historical capabilities; V10's no-stage projection description applies to V10, not this V17 extension.
+
 # V13 accepted-entry original8 routine diagnostic
 
 Separate button under existing --routine-cost installs one own Gltf.prepareFrame waiter. At accepted Actor false-to-true it restores the exact waiter descriptor before synchronously starting the original captureRoutineCost, then calls original prepare once. One arm-time30s deadline covers standby+8 frames including a post-done synchronous check. Original3scope and8routine modules/buttons are byte-exact; they are never generally layered. New optional scalar entryTrigger in existing routine-cost receipt records arm/deadline/trigger/install/terminal times and SceneID correlation; install time is not Scene start. Original routineProfile remains truthful even when its eight frames complete after the outer deadline. Invalid/refused/aborted/foreign/error attempts remain evidence. Coldness needs fresh Game/original session, and profiling includes observer/JIT overhead, not FPS/GPU execution. Existing lifecycle-controls behavior is unchanged. New entry-routine-helper evidence contains primary research, hashes, tests and handoff; root alone builds/runs actual capture.

